From 5059768c1f156ccb54c029696d54ce6dd136e3a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] stream-prefill: stream the CPU experts to the GPU for long
 prefills

`KT_GPU_STREAM_PREFILL=<tokens>`: above that many tokens the CPU experts
are not computed by kt-kernel; their weights are copied to the GPU in
groups and computed there, the copy of the next group overlapping the
compute of the current one (`kt_stream_prefill.py`).
`KT_GPU_STREAM_W16=1` dequantizes each group to bf16 and runs
FlashInfer's bf16 CUTLASS MoE (SM89+); otherwise the SM120 MXFP8 x MXFP4
kernel. `KT_GPU_STREAM_ZEROCOPY` reads kt-kernel's shared expert memory
directly and `KT_GPU_STREAM_GRAPH` launches each group as one CUDA
graph. One CUTLASS MoE workspace per GPU is preallocated before the
decode graphs are captured, for the resident experts as well (this part
is always on), and `KT_GPU_STREAM_ROW_BLOCK` splits long chunks into row
blocks. Also: early streamer init, CPU groups (`KT_STREAM_CPU_GROUPS`),
a reference check (`KT_HOT_CHECK`), and comment updates in the wrapper.

ZEROCOPY with GPUs and kt-kernel NUMA parts that differ in number (one
GPU and two sockets, two GPUs and one socket, NPS2/NPS4 nodes): each rank
reads every part its rows of the intermediate size sit in, and the W16
dequant writes them in place (rows for gate/up, columns for down). Before,
a rank read one part only: one GPU on two sockets ran out of bounds, and
two GPUs on one socket would both have read the first half.

Numerics: Not bit-identical when on: the streamed CPU experts run on the
GPU (W16: bf16 rounding instead of kt-kernel's; the MXFP8 mode has a
larger error). The shared workspace changes memory only. ZEROCOPY needs
the kt-kernel tree patch (`KT_EXPERT_SHM`).

Prerequisites: `prefill-lend`, `loading`, `placement`.

